      <div><h3>Natural Hair</h3><p>A hooded steamer paired with a 20-minute deep conditioning session is the routine most cited by natural hair communities. Look for a model with adjustable steam levels and a chair-friendly height.</p><span class="ks-tag">Hooded steamer recommended</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ks-row">
      <div class="ks-num">Low<br>Por.</div>
      <div><h3>Low Porosity Hair</h3><p>Low porosity hair benefits the most dramatically from steam, because warm vapor helps lift the cuticle that otherwise blocks product penetration. A 15–25 minute steam after applying conditioner can change how moisturized your hair feels for the entire wash week.</p><span class="ks-tag">15–25 min after conditioner</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ks-row">
      <div class="ks-num">2C–3B</div>
      <div><h3>Curly Hair</h3><p>Steam can boost curl definition and reduce frizz by encouraging even product distribution. Lighter, finer curl types often prefer handheld steamers since hooded models can deliver more steam than needed.</p><span class="ks-tag">Handheld often preferred</span></div>
    </div>
