    <div class="ks-step"><div class="ks-snum">01</div><div><h3>Timing</h3><p>15–25 minutes is the sweet spot for most hair types. Longer doesn't mean better — water-logged hair can become more fragile and prone to breakage.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ks-step"><div class="ks-snum">02</div><div><h3>Distance (handheld models)</h3><p>Keep the wand 6–8 inches from your hair. Too close turns steam into water droplets and can flatten curl pattern rather than enhance it.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ks-step"><div class="ks-snum">03</div><div><h3>Product layering</h3><p>Apply your deep conditioner before steaming, not after. Steam's job is to help the product absorb — it works best with something to push in.</p></div></div>
