<!-- ══ FAQ ══ -->
<section class="ks-section ks-pillars-bg" style="{% if section.settings.color_faq != blank %}background-color:{{ section.settings.color_faq }};{% endif %}">
  <div class="ks-center-head">
    <span class="ks-kicker">Questions</span>
    <h2>We've heard <em>these before.</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="ks-faq">
    <div class="ks-faq-item"><button class="ks-faq-q"><span>What does a hair steamer do?</span><span class="ks-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"><line x1="6" y1="0" x2="6" y2="12"/><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="12" y2="6"/></svg></span></button><div class="ks-faq-a"><p>A hair steamer applies warm moisture to your hair to help open the cuticle, allowing conditioners and treatments to absorb more deeply. It supports moisture retention and product penetration, especially for low porosity, curly, and natural hair types.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ks-faq-item"><button class="ks-faq-q"><span>Is a hair steamer worth it?</span><span class="ks-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"><line x1="6" y1="0" x2="6" y2="12"/><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="12" y2="6"/></svg></span></button><div class="ks-faq-a"><p>For people with low porosity, curly, coily, or natural hair who struggle with dryness or product buildup, a hair steamer is one of the most-cited upgrades to a wash-day routine. For straight or already easily-moisturized hair, the benefit is smaller.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ks-faq-item"><button class="ks-faq-q"><span>How often should I steam my hair?</span><span class="ks-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"><line x1="6" y1="0" x2="6" y2="12"/><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="12" y2="6"/></svg></span></button><div class="ks-faq-a"><p>Most users steam once a week, paired with their wash day. Some natural hair routines include a mid-week refresh steam for hydration. Daily steaming is not recommended — too much moisture exposure can over-soften strands.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ks-faq-item"><button class="ks-faq-q"><span>Should I steam before or after washing?</span><span class="ks-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"><line x1="6" y1="0" x2="6" y2="12"/><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="12" y2="6"/></svg></span></button><div class="ks-faq-a"><p>Both work, and serve different purposes. Pre-shampoo steaming (with oil) helps protect strands during cleansing. Post-wash steaming (with deep conditioner) is more common and supports deeper conditioning.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ks-faq-item"><button class="ks-faq-q"><span>Hooded vs. handheld — which should I buy?</span><span class="ks-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"><line x1="6" y1="0" x2="6" y2="12"/><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="12" y2="6"/></svg></span></button><div class="ks-faq-a"><p>A hooded hair steamer is better for long, hands-free deep conditioning sessions and full-coverage steam. A handheld is better for portability, travel, refresh routines, and smaller spaces.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ks-faq-item"><button class="ks-faq-q"><span>Can I use a hair steamer on dry hair?</span><span class="ks-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"><line x1="6" y1="0" x2="6" y2="12"/><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="12" y2="6"/></svg></span></button><div class="ks-faq-a"><p>Yes — many wavy and curly hair users steam dry hair to refresh their style mid-week without re-washing. The steam reactivates products already in your hair and revives curl pattern.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ks-faq-item"><button class="ks-faq-q"><span>Is steaming safe for color-treated hair?</span><span class="ks-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"><line x1="6" y1="0" x2="6" y2="12"/><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="12" y2="6"/></svg></span></button><div class="ks-faq-a"><p>Generally yes. Many colorists recommend it because steam supports moisture retention without exposing color to high dry heat. Keep sessions to 15–20 minutes and wait 48–72 hours after a fresh color appointment.</p></div></div>
    <div class="ks-faq-item"><button class="ks-faq-q"><span>Hair steamer vs. heat cap — what's the difference?</span><span class="ks-faq-icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"><line x1="6" y1="0" x2="6" y2="12"/><line x1="0" y1="6" x2="12" y2="6"/></svg></span></button><div class="ks-faq-a"><p>A heat cap warms your hair using dry heat. A hair steamer adds both heat and moisture. For low porosity and very dry hair, steamers are typically the more effective choice.</p></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

